      "description": "Watch Columbus Crew vs CF Montreal highlights and goals from Major League Soccer on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 20, 2026. The stage was set for a high-stakes MLS encounter on August 20, 2026 , as Columbus Crew hosted CF Montreal . Both sides took to the pitch eager to claim vital points in the league standings, promising a match filled with tactical intrigue and competitive fire. Explosive Start for the Crew The match ignited almost immediately, with Columbus Crew asserting their dominance from the opening whistle. Despite an early yellow card for Rudy Camacho in the 3rd minute, the home side found their rhythm quickly. In the 5th minute, Gennadiy Synchuk delivered a pinpoint assist to Prince Osei Owusu , who clinically found the back of the net to give the Crew an early lead. The momentum stayed firmly with the hosts, and disaster struck for CF Montreal in the 20th minute when goalkeeper Thomas Gillier inadvertently sent the ball into his own net, doubling the advantage for the home side. Physical Battles and Tactical Adjustments As the game progressed into the second half, the intensity remained high, leading to a flurry of yellow cards for players like Andre Gomes , Jalen Neal , and Brayan Ceballos . CF Montreal attempted to shift the tide with several substitutions, introducing Josef Martinez and Marcelo Herrera to find a spark. However, the Columbus Crew defense held firm, effectively neutralizing the visitors' attacks while managing the tempo of the game through disciplined midfield play and strategic ball retention. Sealing the Victory The knockout blow arrived in the 78th minute when Noah Streit clinical finish made it three for the hosts, effectively ending any hopes of a Montreal comeback. Following the goal, the Crew introduced fresh legs including Alexis Sanchez and Daniel Gazdag to see out the match. The final whistle blew after eight minutes of stoppage time, marking a comprehensive victory for Columbus Crew in front of their home supporters."
